"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Favorable findings include negative surgical margins, absence of seminal vesicle invasion, and lack of lymphovascular invasion. The preoperative PSA was elevated at 8.4. The surgical pathology showed a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and pathological T2 stage with no extraprostatic extension. Countervailing factors include the absence of lymph node removal, resulting in an uncharacterized nodal status, which widens uncertainty. Furthermore, the biopsy showed a progression from Gleason 0+0 to 3+4 over time. The absence of postoperative PSA or follow-up data prevents a definitive assessment of recurrence risk trajectory. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and subsequent trajectory would significantly revise this prognosis. The current heuristic horizon suggests a potential recurrence window. The fixed estimated horizon is 87.65 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 56.97–118.32 months; its coverage has not been validated."
